## First steps

1. Initialize git with `git init -b main` if needed.
2. Switch Codex to this generated repo and keep the product conversation here instead of HQ.
3. Use `{{DEFAULT_NODE_VERSION}}` before running npm commands. The repo includes `.nvmrc` and `.node-version`.
4. Set the local git hooks path with `git config core.hooksPath .githooks`.
5. Enable the commit template with `git config commit.template .gitmessage.txt`.
6. Keep the main branch name as `main`.
7. Create a branch such as `feature/init`.
8. Read `DESIGN.md`, `docs/prompting/prompt-context.kr.md`, `docs/design/art-direction.kr.md`, `docs/design/design-reference-selection.kr.md`, `docs/design/ui-principles.kr.md`, and `docs/design/browser-review.kr.md`.
9. For serious UI work, also read `docs/design/ui-intent-brief.kr.md`, `docs/design/layout-exploration.kr.md`, `docs/design/visual-concepts.kr.md`, and `docs/prompting/ui-foundation-prompt-template.kr.md`.
10. For narrow UI edits, read `docs/design/ui-edit-brief.kr.md` and `docs/prompting/ui-edit-prompt-template.kr.md`.
11. Run `python3 scripts/harness.py pre-task`.
12. Start the first implementation slice described in `docs/exec-plans/active/{{BOOTSTRAP_TASK_ID}}.kr.md`.
13. For UI or flow work, review the running app in a browser before treating the result as complete.

## Required artifacts

- Task plan before editing
